					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quikngruvn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(333389); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=333389&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608608523" alt="Quikngruvn" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=333389)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/quikngruvn" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(333389); return false;" >Quikngruvn</a></span> <span class="odate time_1314458096 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">27 Aug 2011 15:14</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1241807">
									

<p>First off, I had given this about even odds that it was going to be downvoted to oblivion for being too silly, so having it reach double digits is a pleasant surprise, to say the least. Turns out that trying to describe a magic spell without using either &quot;magic&quot; or &quot;spell&quot; is hard to do. Also, I wasn't consciously trying to, but I managed to not expunge anything, for whatever it's worth.</p>
<p>moose, I thought about it, and I still want to stay away from using actual D&amp;D spell names. I think they would detract more than they'd add, IMO. 'Sides, <a href="/scp-846">Robo-Dude</a> has that covered already.</p>
<p>Sal, um&#8230; an object that lets you summon a critter out of thin air is &quot;mundane&quot;? Or is that just by Foundation standards, which&#8230; I can't really argue. But Rhett's got in it that this is, really, the Basic Set. Figure, IRL there were eventually five sets of rules for D&amp;D for increasingly-powerful characters (Basic, Expert, Companion, Master, and Immortal), so there may very well be five analogous volumes of spell books&#8230;. But, you gotta crawl before you can walk, and so I didn't want to make the effects here at all powerful.</p>
<p>Kerlyssa, D&amp;D was also supposedly a gateway to witchcraft and the occult, in addition to Satanism, and I decided to go with magic in general, from&#8230; some unspecified source. Making it Satanic in nature would have imposed religiosity on it (since Satan is specifically a Judeo-Christian concept) that, frankly, would not have worked at all.</p>
<p>Ker/Eric, I can certainly see how this could be a -J&#8230; but if I were trying to make it a -J, I would have gone for over the top instead of subdued. As it is, it's right where it belongs (or will be, once it gets its number).</p>
<p>Severe, crap, I had totally forgotten about 433 when I wrote this up. I <em>think</em> mine is different enough from yours to stand on its own, but I can definitely see the similarities.</p>
<p>And as always, thanks to everyone for reading, voting, and commenting.</p>
<p>(That turned out longer than expected. Ah well.)</p>

